class:: VisualSynthDef
summary:: A visual instrument definition (render function + default params + envelope)
categories:: Libraries>VisualServer
related:: Classes/VisualServer, Classes/Vbind, Guides/VisualServer, Reference/VisualParameters

description::

Defines how a visual node is drawn each frame, analogous to a link::Classes/SynthDef:: for audio. A def has a name, a render link::Classes/Function:: code::{ |node, view, elapsed, centerX, centerY, params| ... }::, and a default-parameter link::Classes/Event::.

All defs are registered in code::*initClass:: via link::#*initBuiltInDefs::; look them up with link::#*at::. Coordinates are normalised code::-1.0 .. 1.0:: relative to the view centre.

subsection:: Built-in defs

table::
## strong::name:: || strong::default params::
## code::\circle::  || code::(x: 0, y: 0, size: 50, color: Color.white, dur: 1, fill: true)::
## code::\square::  || code::(x: 0, y: 0, size: 50, color: Color.white, dur: 1, fill: true)::
## code::\line::    || code::(x1: -0.5, y1: 0, x2: 0.5, y2: 0, color: Color.white, width: 1, dur: 1)::
## code::\pulse::   || code::(x: 0, y: 0, startSize: 10, endSize: 100, color: Color.white, dur: 1, curve: \exp)::
## code::\spinner:: || code::(x: 0, y: 0, length: 50, color: Color.white, speed: 1, dur: inf, width: 2)::
## code::\live::    || code::(x: 0, y: 0, size: 50, color: Color.white, dur: inf, fill: true)::
::

See link::Reference/VisualParameters:: for the meaning of every key.

subsection:: Envelope / lifetime model

Every def's lifetime and alpha/scale come from link::#-envState::. The node's life is decoupled from the pattern's code::\dur:: (event spacing):

code::
life = (sustain ? dur) * legato * stretch
::

with an code::[attack, hold, release]:: envelope spanning that life. Defaults (code::legato:: 1, code::stretch:: 1, code::attack:: 0, code::release:: nil, code::sustain:: nil) reproduce the original "fade 1->0 over code::dur::, free at code::dur::" behaviour. code::life == inf:: => persistent node (e.g. code::\live::, code::\spinner::). Set code::\legato:: or code::\sustain:: to make animations overlap. See link::Guides/VisualServer:: §Envelope.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create and register a def.
argument:: name
A link::Classes/Symbol::.
argument:: renderFunc
code::{ |node, view, elapsed, centerX, centerY, params| ... }::. Use code::node[\def].getParam(node, \key, default):: to read params and link::#-envState:: for alpha/scale/expiry. Do not use code::^:: in this function (out-of-context return).
argument:: defaultParams
An link::Classes/Event:: of default key/value pairs.

method:: at
Look up a registered def by name.
argument:: name
The def symbol. Returns code::nil:: if not found.

method:: initBuiltInDefs
Register the six built-in defs. Called from code::*initClass::; also re-called defensively by link::Classes/VisualServer::'s code::init:: if the registry is empty.

method:: all
The link::Classes/Dictionary:: of name -> def.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

method:: getParam
Read a node parameter, falling back to this def's defaults then code::default::. link::Classes/Function::-valued params are evaluated every call (live input).
argument:: node
The node event.
argument:: key
Parameter symbol.
argument:: default
Fallback if unset.

method:: numParam
Like link::#-getParam:: but strictly numeric: any non-number (e.g. an inherited code::sustain:: Function) falls back to code::default::. Used by link::#-envState:: for timing keys.
argument:: node
argument:: key
argument:: default

method:: envState
Per-frame envelope state for a node. Returns an link::Classes/Event:: code::(alpha:, scale:, expired:, life:)::.
argument:: node
The node event.
argument:: elapsed
Seconds since the node started.
discussion::
code::life = (sustain ? dur) * legato * stretch::; code::life == inf:: returns code::(alpha: 1, scale: 1, expired: false, life: inf)::. Otherwise builds code::Env([0,1,1,0], [attack, hold, release], curve):: and samples it at code::elapsed::.

method:: calcEnv
Map code::(elapsed/duration).clip(0,1):: through a curve symbol (code::\linear \sin \cos \exp \log::). Used by code::\pulse:: for its size sweep.
argument:: elapsed
argument:: duration
argument:: curve

method:: envCurve
Map a curve symbol to an link::Classes/Env::-safe curve: code::\exp:: -> code::-4::, code::\log:: -> code::4:: (Env exp segments cannot touch level 0), code::\sin::/code::\linear:: pass through, default code::\sin::.
argument:: sym

method:: name
method:: renderFunc
method:: defaultParams

EXAMPLES::

code::
VisualSynthDef(\ring, { |node, view, elapsed, centerX, centerY, params|
    var def = node[\def];
    var st  = def.envState(node, elapsed);
    if (st[\expired]) {
        VisualServer.default.vfree(node[\nodeID]);
    } {
        var x = def.getParam(node, \x, 0) * centerX + centerX;
        var y = def.getParam(node, \y, 0) * centerY + centerY;
        var s = def.getParam(node, \size, 60) * st[\scale];
        Pen.strokeColor = def.getParam(node, \color, Color.white).copy.alpha_(st[\alpha]);
        Pen.width = 4;
        Pen.addOval(Rect(x - (s/2), y - (s/2), s, s));
        Pen.stroke;
    };
}, (x: 0, y: 0, size: 60, color: Color.white, dur: 1));

VisualServer.default.vnew(\ring, nil, \demo, [\size, 120, \dur, 2, \legato, 3]);
::
